    "created_at": "2020-06-17T20:14:25Z",
    "updated_at": "2020-06-17T20:14:25Z",
    "body": "I'll add another use case: We have a free application we'll give you in return for getting your email. Unabashed lead generation, yes, but it gives you something of value in return for your info, and does nothing unless you click.\r\n\r\nTrue it's not vital to this use case. But in these days of third party javascript libraries, I'd far prefer it allow only the download you click on. That will build an extra firewall as one more hurdle for malice to clear if one of the third-party library providers has, um, an accident. I'm after anything I can do to stop someone stuffing something into potential customers systems.",
